# What must NOT reach the build context.
#
# The first entry is load-bearing rather than a size optimisation. The Dockerfile
# runs `npm ci --omit=dev` and then `COPY . .`; if node_modules came along, that
# copy would paste a Windows developer's @img/sharp-win32-x64 over the Linux
# binaries just installed, and sharp would throw the moment documentScan.js is
# imported. The same applies to any native module.
node_modules
npm-debug.log*

# No secret is ever baked into a layer. Cloud Run gets these from Secret Manager
# and the environment; an image is a file anybody with pull access can unpack.
.env
.env.*

# Not needed at runtime and each one is a reason to rebuild a layer.
tests
scripts/free-port.js
.git
.gitignore
.vscode
.idea
common-cmds.txt
DEPLOY.md

# NOTHING ELSE. In particular, these must stay in the image and are listed here
# only so a future edit does not delete them by accident:
#
#   data/           zones.geojson and shady-zones.geojson are read at runtime by
#                   services/fareZones.js and services/safeRoute.js, resolved
#                   relative to import.meta.url. Without them the server boots
#                   and then fails on the first fare quote.
#   prisma/         schema.prisma is read by the client at import.
#   tsconfig.json   tsx reads it to resolve the .ts route files.
